```

A few deliberate choices:

- I have **not** ignored `.joblib`, `.pt`, `.json`, `.csv`, `.png`, `.npz` or notebooks globally.
- Your trained models remain available through Git LFS.
- The two incomplete comparison directories remain on your computer but won't be included in the initial repository.
- Your final curated figures can be retained in `outputs/figures/`.
- Your experimental reports remain available for reproducibility.

GitHub currently warns for ordinary Git files above 50 MiB and blocks files above 100 MiB. Git LFS is the correct approach for your large model artifacts. GitHub Free currently provides 10 GiB of LFS storage and bandwidth, with a 2 GiB individual LFS-file limit. <Cite refs={["turn510062search0","turn510062search5","turn510062search3"]}/>

---

# 3. Apply the `.gitignore`

Paste this into PowerShell to save the contents from the code block above:

```powershell
notepad .gitignore
```

Replace everything, save and close.

Then check the important rules:

```powershell
git check-ignore -v .venv/
git check-ignore -v .pytest_cache/
git check-ignore -v data/processed/unet_cache/manifest.json
git check-ignore -v db/project_quantum.sqlite3
git check-ignore -v data/raw/Task01_BrainTumour/dataset.json
git check-ignore -v PROJECT_QUANTUM_V3_SUBMISSION_FACULTY_GITHUB.zip
```

Then verify that the models are still tracked by Git LFS:

```powershell
git check-attr filter -- artifacts/msd_rf_16.joblib
git check-attr filter -- artifacts/msd_rf_32.joblib
git check-attr filter -- artifacts/msd_rf_240.joblib
git check-attr filter -- artifacts/msd_unet_240.pt

Get-Content .gitattributes
```

Expected attribute:

```text
filter: lfs
```

# 4. Check the repository before staging

Run:

```powershell
git status --short
```

And inspect all ignored and untracked items:

```powershell
git status --short --ignored
```

Also check for large experimental files:

```powershell
Get-ChildItem . -File -Recurse -Force |
    Where-Object {
        $_.Length -gt 50MB -and
        $_.FullName -notmatch '[\\/](\.git|\.venv|venv|data[\\/]raw)[\\/]'
    } |
    Select-Object FullName, @{
        Name = "Size_MB"
        Expression = { [math]::Round($_.Length / 1MB, 2) }
    } |
    Sort-Object Size_MB -Descending |
    Format-Table -AutoSize
```

The large model files should be LFS-tracked. The faculty ZIP should be ignored.

